    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "0fbd4f7716134eb3d5b35cf6076d51b8cb9a9e1e86a650094eaa8d37cd742116",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw68in5r-zvisk2bzcb-amanda",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The matching Word paragraph names Palacio de Sal alone. It has no equivalent for the current RU day with both hotel options, so the current arrangement is retained."
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the bus station at 07:00 for the roughly three-hour journey to Potosí.\n\nThe Cerro Rico tour begins at 10:30 at the mining market, where your guide explains the use of coca and dynamite and introduces local mining customs. Then enter the mine to see its different levels, watch the miners at work and see the offerings to El Tío, the mine’s deity. Inside the working mine, you can see how long-standing rituals coexist with the demands of daily work.\n\nAfter returning to Potosí, take the bus to Uyuni, a journey of about four hours. On arrival, transfer to Palacio de Sal or Luna Salada."
    },
